{"type":"standard","title":"Mike Flood (politician)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mike Flood (politician)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q6846855","titles":{"canonical":"Mike_Flood_(politician)","normalized":"Mike Flood (politician)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mike Flood (politician)</span></span>"},"pageid":4472435,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Mike_Flood%2C_official_portrait_%28118th_Congress%29.jpg/330px-Mike_Flood%2C_official_portrait_%28118th_Congress%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Mike_Flood%2C_official_portrait_%28118th_Congress%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2500,"height":3125},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376721309","tid":"10fd5a4b-b92a-11f1-b3b8-8d538a7e48b8","timestamp":"2026-09-25T21:42:55Z","description":"American politician (born 1975)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Flood_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Flood_(politician)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Flood_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mike_Flood_(politician)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Flood_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Mike_Flood_(politician)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Flood_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mike_Flood_(politician)"}},"extract":"Michael John Flood is an American attorney, businessman, and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Nebraska's 1st congressional district since July 2022. A member of the Republican Party, he previously served two terms as a member of the Nebraska Legislature from the 19th district, from 2005 to 2013 and 2021 to 2022. He served as speaker of the legislature from 2007 to 2013.","extract_html":"<p><b>Michael John Flood</b> is an American attorney, businessman, and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Nebraska's 1st congressional district since July 2022. A member of the Republican Party, he previously served two terms as a member of the Nebraska Legislature from the 19th district, from 2005 to 2013 and 2021 to 2022. He served as speaker of the legislature from 2007 to 2013.</p>"}